.TH "LIST-BUCKET-INTELLIGENT-TIERING-CONFIGURATIONS"  "" "" ""
.SH NAME
list-bucket-intelligent-tiering-configurations \- 
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This operation is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Lists the S3 Intelligent\-Tiering configuration from the specified bucket.
.sp
The S3 Intelligent\-Tiering storage class is designed to optimize storage costs by automatically moving data to the most cost\-effective storage access tier, without performance impact or operational overhead. S3 Intelligent\-Tiering delivers automatic cost savings in three low latency and high throughput access tiers. To get the lowest storage cost on data that can be accessed in minutes to hours, you can choose to activate additional archiving capabilities.
.sp
The S3 Intelligent\-Tiering storage class is the ideal storage class for data with unknown, changing, or unpredictable access patterns, independent of object size or retention period. If the size of an object is less than 128 KB, it is not monitored and not eligible for auto\-tiering. Smaller objects can be stored, but they are always charged at the Frequent Access tier rates in the S3 Intelligent\-Tiering storage class.
.sp
For more information, see \fI\%Storage class for automatically optimizing frequently and infrequently accessed objects\fP .
.sp
Operations related to \fBListBucketIntelligentTieringConfigurations\fP include:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%DeleteBucketIntelligentTieringConfiguration\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%PutBucketIntelligentTieringConfiguration\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%GetBucketIntelligentTieringConfiguration\fP
.UNINDENT
.sp
See also: AWS API Documentation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
  list\-bucket\-intelligent\-tiering\-configurations
\-\-bucket <value>
[\-\-continuation\-token <value>]
[\-\-expected\-bucket\-owner <value>]
[\-\-cli\-input\-json | \-\-cli\-input\-yaml]
[\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton <value>]
[\-\-debug]
[\-\-endpoint\-url <value>]
[\-\-no\-verify\-ssl]
[\-\-no\-paginate]
[\-\-output <value>]
[\-\-query <value>]
[\-\-profile <value>]
[\-\-region <value>]
[\-\-version <value>]
[\-\-color <value>]
[\-\-no\-sign\-request]
[\-\-ca\-bundle <value>]
[\-\-cli\-read\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-connect\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-binary\-format <value>]
[\-\-no\-cli\-pager]
[\-\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
[\-\-no\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH OPTIONS
.sp
\fB\-\-bucket\fP (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The name of the Amazon S3 bucket whose configuration you want to modify or retrieve.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-continuation\-token\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The \fBContinuationToken\fP that represents a placeholder from where this request should begin.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-expected\-bucket\-owner\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The account ID of the expected bucket owner. If the account ID that you provide does not match the actual owner of the bucket, the request fails with the HTTP status code \fB403 Forbidden\fP (access denied).
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-input\-json\fP | \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP (string)
Reads arguments from the JSON string provided. The JSON string follows the format provided by \fB\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton\fP\&. If other arguments are provided on the command line, those values will override the JSON\-provided values. It is not possible to pass arbitrary binary values using a JSON\-provided value as the string will be taken literally. This may not be specified along with \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP\&.
.sp
\fB\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton\fP (string)
Prints a JSON skeleton to standard output without sending an API request. If provided with no value or the value \fBinput\fP, prints a sample input JSON that can be used as an argument for \fB\-\-cli\-input\-json\fP\&. Similarly, if provided \fByaml\-input\fP it will print a sample input YAML that can be used with \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP\&. If provided with the value \fBoutput\fP, it validates the command inputs and returns a sample output JSON for that command. The generated JSON skeleton is not stable between versions of the AWS CLI and there are no backwards compatibility guarantees in the JSON skeleton generated.
