.SH EXAMPLES
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
To use the following examples, you must have the AWS CLI installed and configured. See the \fI\%Getting started guide\fP in the \fIAWS CLI User Guide\fP for more information.
.sp
Unless otherwise stated, all examples have unix\-like quotation rules. These examples will need to be adapted to your terminal\(aqs quoting rules. See \fI\%Using quotation marks with strings\fP in the \fIAWS CLI User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBTo retrieve all S3 Intelligent\-Tiering configurations on a bucket\fP
.sp
The following \fBlist\-bucket\-intelligent\-tiering\-configurations\fP example retrieves all S3 Intelligent\-Tiering configuration on a bucket.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
aws s3api list\-bucket\-intelligent\-tiering\-configurations \e
    \-\-bucket amzn\-s3\-demo\-bucket
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Output:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
{
    \(dqIsTruncated\(dq: false,
    \(dqIntelligentTieringConfigurationList\(dq: [
        {
            \(dqId\(dq: \(dqExampleConfig\(dq,
            \(dqFilter\(dq: {
                \(dqPrefix\(dq: \(dqimages\(dq
            },
            \(dqStatus\(dq: \(dqEnabled\(dq,
            \(dqTierings\(dq: [
                {
                    \(dqDays\(dq: 90,
                    \(dqAccessTier\(dq: \(dqARCHIVE_ACCESS\(dq
                },
                {
                    \(dqDays\(dq: 180,
                    \(dqAccessTier\(dq: \(dqDEEP_ARCHIVE_ACCESS\(dq
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            \(dqId\(dq: \(dqExampleConfig2\(dq,
            \(dqStatus\(dq: \(dqDisabled\(dq,
            \(dqTierings\(dq: [
                {
                    \(dqDays\(dq: 730,
                    \(dqAccessTier\(dq: \(dqARCHIVE_ACCESS\(dq
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            \(dqId\(dq: \(dqExampleConfig3\(dq,
            \(dqFilter\(dq: {
                \(dqTag\(dq: {
                    \(dqKey\(dq: \(dqdocuments\(dq,
                    \(dqValue\(dq: \(dqtaxes\(dq
                }
            },
            \(dqStatus\(dq: \(dqEnabled\(dq,
            \(dqTierings\(dq: [
                {
                    \(dqDays\(dq: 90,
                    \(dqAccessTier\(dq: \(dqARCHIVE_ACCESS\(dq
                },
                {
                    \(dqDays\(dq: 365,
                    \(dqAccessTier\(dq: \(dqDEEP_ARCHIVE_ACCESS\(dq
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
For more information, see \fI\%Using S3 Intelligent\-Tiering\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP\&.
.SH OUTPUT
.sp
IsTruncated \-> (boolean)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Indicates whether the returned list of analytics configurations is complete. A value of \fBtrue\fP indicates that the list is not complete and the \fBNextContinuationToken\fP will be provided for a subsequent request.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ContinuationToken \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The \fBContinuationToken\fP that represents a placeholder from where this request should begin.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
NextContinuationToken \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The marker used to continue this inventory configuration listing. Use the \fBNextContinuationToken\fP from this response to continue the listing in a subsequent request. The continuation token is an opaque value that Amazon S3 understands.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
IntelligentTieringConfigurationList \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The list of S3 Intelligent\-Tiering configurations for a bucket.
.sp
(structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the S3 Intelligent\-Tiering configuration for an Amazon S3 bucket.
.sp
For information about the S3 Intelligent\-Tiering storage class, see \fI\%Storage class for automatically optimizing frequently and infrequently accessed objects\fP .
.sp
Id \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The ID used to identify the S3 Intelligent\-Tiering configuration.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Filter \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies a bucket filter. The configuration only includes objects that meet the filter\(aqs criteria.
.sp
Prefix \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
An object key name prefix that identifies the subset of objects to which the rule applies.
.sp
\fBWARNING:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
